evidence.quote:
For $N=N_\Sigma$ on $X_\Sigma$, or $N=N_J$ on $X_J$, one has $$\label{rec:sum-modulus}
 \widehat\delta_N(t)\ge t^3/128\qquad(0<t<1).$$ For $X_0$, a finite initial set $H$, a vector $x$ supported in $H$, and $z\in F_H\setminus\{0\}$, one has $$\label{rec:equal-estimate}
 \frac{N_0(x+z)+N_0(x-z)}2\ge N_0(x)
 +\frac{N_0(z)^3}{8(2N_0(x)+N_0(z))^2}.$$ Each of $X_\Sigma,X_0,X_J$ admits no equivalent AUC norm.

hypotheses.statement:
For $N=N_\Sigma$ on $X_\Sigma$, or $N=N_J$ on $X_J$, one has $$\label{rec:sum-modulus}
 \widehat\delta_N(t)\ge t^3/128\qquad(0<t<1).$$ For $X_0$, a finite initial set $H$, a vector $x$ supported in $H$, and $z\in F_H\setminus\{0\}$, one has $$\label{rec:equal-estimate}
 \frac{N_0(x+z)+N_0(x-z)}2\ge N_0(x)
 +\frac{N_0(z)^3}{8(2N_0(x)+N_0(z))^2}.$$ Each of $X_\Sigma,X_0,X_J$ admits no equivalent AUC norm.

For every $\varepsilon>0$ there is $\eta(\varepsilon)\in(0,1)$ such that, for $x,z_1,z_2,\ldots\in X_J$, $$\left.
 \begin{gathered}
 N_J(x+z_j),N_J(x-z_j)\le1\quad(j\ge1),\\
 N_J(z_i-z_j)\ge\varepsilon\quad(i\ne j)
 \end{gathered}
 \right\}
 \quad\Longrightarrow\quad N_J(x)\le1-\eta(\varepsilon).$$ For $0<\varepsilon\le2$, one can take $\eta(\varepsilon)=\min\{1/2,\gamma(2,\varepsilon/16)\}$.

Let $x,y\in E_h$, with $x$ supported on a finite ancestral set $A$ and $y$ zero on $A$. Put $M_\sigma=
u_h(x+\sigma y)$, $B=
u_h(x)$, and $M=\max\{M_+,M_-\}$. If $M>0$, then $$\label{var:cubic-component-eq}
  rac{M_++M_-}{2}-B
 \ge c_3 rac{
u_h(y)^3}{M^2},\qquad c_3=(6\mathrm e)^{-3}.$$ This also holds for $x=0$ and arbitrary $y$. When $M=0$, both vectors are zero.

Let $x\in X_{\mathrm v}$ and $0<\varepsilon\le1$. Suppose $(y_j)$ is weakly null, $\|y_j\|_{\mathrm v}\ge\varepsilon$, and $\|x+y_j\|_{\mathrm v},\|x-y_j\|_{\mathrm v}\le1$ for every $j$. Then $$\label{var:theta}
 \|x\|_{\mathrm v}\le\theta(\varepsilon)
 :=\left(1-\frac{c_3}{2\sqrt2}\varepsilon^3\right)^{1/2}<1.$$

